i2c_hid: snooze when there is no input-ready line

On some trackpads (XPS 15 9560) InputReadyLine::Init fails, so
fInputReady stays NULL. MaybeScheduleTransfer then re-reads the input
register on every call. The device returns the previous report and the
input_server watcher never sleeps.

Add a short snooze in that case so the core stays idle. Reports are
still delivered, so constant-speed motion works. The cursor still drifts
after the finger lifts; that needs the ready line.

See https://github.com/RenkuOS/Source/issues/702
